hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16019","Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Alqamah, from Salamah ibn Yazid al-Jufi, he said, I and my brother went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said, we said, O Messenger of Allah, our mother Mulaykah used to keep kinship ties and honor the guest and do this and that, she died in the pre-Islamic age, does that benefit her at all, he said: No. He said, we said, and she had buried alive a sister of ours in the pre-Islamic age, does that benefit her at all, he said: The woman who buries alive and the buried infant are in the Fire, unless the burying woman attains Islam and Allah pardons her."
